/-!
# The cases

`parts` lists the cubes, in the groups that one module each refutes: `E670/Part/Pk.lean` refutes
`parts[k]!`.  The literal `pos x y z` says `x ◇ y = z` and `neg x y z` says `x ◇ y ≠ z`.

This file is data and is not trusted: `E670.Main` checks that no model of the formula avoids all
the cubes.
The cubes were found by a search that fixes entries of the first row and then of the first column
until CaDiCaL refutes the case within a few seconds.
-/

